{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1326","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Maximums"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alicia has an array, $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$, of non-negative integers. For each $$$1 \\leq i \\leq n$$$, she has found a non-negative integer $$$x_i = max(0, a_1, \\ldots, a_{i-1})$$$. Note that for $$$i=1$$$, $$$x_i = 0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if Alicia had the array $$$a = \\{0, 1, 2, 0, 3\\}$$$, then $$$x = \\{0, 0, 1, 2, 2\\}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, she calculated an array, $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$: $$$b_i = a_i - x_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if Alicia had the array $$$a = \\{0, 1, 2, 0, 3\\}$$$, $$$b = \\{0-0, 1-0, 2-1, 0-2, 3-2\\} = \\{0, 1, 1, -2, 1\\}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alicia gives you the values $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$ and asks you to restore the values $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$. Can you help her solve the problem?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\leq n \\leq 200\\,000$$$) – the number of elements in Alicia's array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next line contains $$$n$$$ integers, $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\leq b_i \\leq 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that for the given array $$$b$$$ there is a solution $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$, for all elements of which the following is true: $$$0 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$n$$$ integers, $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$), such that if you calculate $$$x$$$ according to the statement, $$$b_1$$$ will be equal to $$$a_1 - x_1$$$, $$$b_2$$$ will be equal to $$$a_2 - x_2$$$, ..., and $$$b_n$$$ will be equal to $$$a_n - x_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that there exists at least one solution for the given tests. It can be shown that the solution is unique."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n0 1 1 -2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0 1 2 0 3 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1000 999999000 -1000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1000 1000000000 0 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2 1 2 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 3 5 7 10 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first test was described in the problem statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test, if Alicia had an array $$$a = \\{1000, 1000000000, 0\\}$$$, then $$$x = \\{0, 1000, 1000000000\\}$$$ and $$$b = \\{1000-0, 1000000000-1000, 0-1000000000\\} = \\{1000, 999999000, -1000000000\\}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1326B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1326/problem/B"}